{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "process-brakewear-runspec",
    "description": "PLAN.md §7.5 step 7d, the POLLUTANT dimension again: the `process-brakewear` RunSpec -- brake-wear PM2.5 and PM10 and running-exhaust Total Energy Consumption -- computed from the DEFAULT DATABASE. It mounts `moves-onroad.esm` and supplies the fourteen things that are this run's: thirteen runspec selections and the expected output. It is the eighth RunSpec this domain document reproduces and it needed NO CHANGE TO THE MODEL: it was written by copying `runspecs/process-tirewear.esm` and swapping fourteen `url_template`s, and it reproduced all 375 cells on the first run.\n\nTHAT IS THE RESULT, and a RunSpec that costs nothing to add is worth adding only if it can fail, so here is what it would have caught (§23).\n\n* THE MODEL-YEAR GROUP IS NOT 0 HERE, AND IT IS 0 EVERYWHERE ELSE IN THIS DIRECTORY. `rt_modelYearGroupIsPresent` (J18, J19) is S10's two inner joins as one semi-join: `pollutantprocessmodelyear` must carry the (polProcessID, modelYearID) pair AND its group must be a `modelyeargroup` row. For PM10 tire wear that group is 0 for all 41 model years -- 0 is itself a `modelyeargroup` row, named `Doesn't Matter`, which is the only reason the tire-wear path passes the test at all. For PM10 BRAKE wear it is six real groups, 19501980 through 20112020, short groups 1 to 6, and the model year the run emits decides which. This is the first run in the corpus where that join has to find anything.\n\n* IT IS A SECOND PROCESS ON THE `emissionRate` ARM. Process 9 rather than process 10, a disjoint set of rate rows, and the same spine: the arm selection J58 added is exercised by a pollutant-process it was not written against.\n\n* THE CHAIN IS THE SAME SHAPE AND A DIFFERENT PAIR. `runspecchainedto` here says 10609 <- 11609, PM2.5 brake wear out of PM10 brake wear, where tire wear says 10710 <- 11710; the chained block carries no rate of its own and is emitted anyway, which is the rule J77 wrote.\n\nWHAT IT DOES NOT DISCRIMINATE, said plainly because it is most of the document: county, month, day, hour, source type, road type and the fuel types are `process-tirewear`'s, unchanged, and so are all four declared shape numbers -- `n_outputPolProcess` 3, `n_outputCohort` 125, `n_sourceBin` 1, `n_physicsRow` 1, every one of them left at its default. The dimension under test is the pollutant and nothing else moves.\n\n375 rows, worst cell 8.251e-06 against the run's own MOVESOutput.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "runspec",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "process-brakewear",
      "brake-wear"
    ]
  },
